'WHAT HAPPENED BEFORE
Black Friday 2024: a sitewide markdown. BF week $110k on $32k spend (3.5x). Black Friday itself 329 orders, $47k.
Black Friday 2025: 30% off sitewide from Nov 15 ("early BF"), nothing moved until the weekend. Friday 186 orders, $26.7k. Saturday fell to $12k, so the site went to 50% off everything Saturday night. Cyber Monday was the best day at $26.8k. BF week $72k on the SAME $32k spend (2.2x). Down 35% on a deeper discount.
What sold: the LGW01 Gold wedge was 44% of the weekend (348 units), then the Eclipse putters. 75 to 85% of weekend buyers were new.
Competitors on the day: Vice up to 50% off, Stix 30% sitewide, Macade 3 for 2. Takomo holds price ("premium wedges, honest price") and that is the lane we picked on Sep 8: same quality, fair price, never cut the club.

THE 2026 PLAN, JUDGED
No markdown, free hat with any club, first 400 orders a polo, members shop Thursday. It is the right brand move and it is also the smallest Black Friday offer Lucky has ever run: a hat is about $25 of value on a $135 wedge, against the 30 to 50% people saw the last two years and every golf competitor shows on the day. On its own it will not beat 2025''s weekend. The plan already knows this: Plan B (buy 2 clubs, get a Carver 02 Gold free, about a third off a 3-club basket) is the Black-Friday-grade offer, held behind a Friday 2pm trigger.

RECOMMENDATION
1. Lead with the bundle from Friday 8am, not at 2pm: "Buy any 2 clubs, get a Carver 02 Gold free. Every club comes with a free hat. First 400 orders get a polo." The story stays "prices never drop, we add to the box".
2. Cyber Monday needs its own step up (2025''s best day was Monday at 50% off). Keep it in the no-markdown family: add the glove to every order, or "buy 2, pick ANY third club free".
3. Thursday for members stays: it is what the giveaway is for. The giveaway size is the real KPI for a no-discount weekend. Set a target (5,000 entries) and watch it weekly.
4. Weekend goal: $100k Fri to Mon (between 2024''s $119k and 2025''s $83k) on about $35k spend, 2.9x. Ladder: breakeven 1.56, target 3.0, scale 50% at 3.5, scale 100% at 4.0. Starting budget $10k; 2024 hit the $13k Meta cap on Friday, so ask for the limit increase the week of Nov 9.
5. If Friday 2pm is under $9k with the bundle already live, the fallback is a markdown on wedges only (30% off LGW01 and LGW02), never sitewide.');
